# Code Review

Establish the requested baseline. Read `AGENTS.md`, the approved task contract,
`docs/CHANGE_IMPACT.md`, and only the relevant authority documents. Inspect
starting status before the diff so existing work is not misattributed. Review
tracked, staged, and relevant untracked changes.

For every new or materially changed source file, identify its language/module
and apply the corresponding industry profile from `docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md`.
Treat verified compiler, build, CI, security/privacy, compatibility, and public-
contract requirements as hard constraints. Existing local conventions remain
compatibility evidence but do not automatically override the industry baseline.

Check whether `.agents/ai/project-map.json` and
`.agents/ai/verification-routes.json` remain synchronized with changed module
boundaries, public contracts, generated paths, and verification commands.

First compare the diff with the approved files, modules, behaviors, and
non-goals. Treat approval-gate or project-boundary violations as blocking.
Trace changed behavior through callers, consumers, public contracts, data,
configuration, deployment, and documentation. Prioritize user-visible failures,
crashes/data loss, contract and compatibility breaks, security/privacy issues,
concurrency/resource bugs, architecture violations, and missing regression
tests. Review naming, API clarity, dependency direction, design-pattern fit,
nesting, function/file responsibility, cancellation, and resource ownership
against the selected profile. Ignore purely subjective taste that is unsupported
by the profile, project evidence, or a concrete readability/maintenance impact.

Identify substantially repeated manual edits or review corrections. At three or
more occurrences, or when recurrence across tasks is evidenced, report a
`docs/CODING_RULES_LOG.md` candidate with scope, examples, replacement, conflicts,
and the best enforcement route. Review-only work does not authorize recording,
tool changes, or historical migration.

For claimed token or speed improvements, verify the proxy definition and
baseline in `docs/AI_PERFORMANCE_BUDGET.md`; reject gains that weaken approval,
consumer/contract coverage, security/privacy, or required verification.

Report actionable findings first, ordered P0 to P3, with precise location,
trigger, impact, violated rule, and safe direction or exception. Do not edit
unless asked; a review-only request never authorizes fixes. If there are no
findings, state reviewed scope, consumer/contract coverage, tests observed or
not run, and residual risks. Repository rules supplement rather than replace
deterministic tests, linters, and required approvals.
